      "content": "Definition: Understandability refers to how easily developers can comprehend and maintain the test code.\n\nTask: Improve the understandability of the test `SoundexTest_testWikipediaAmericanSoundex.java` (path:- /Users/tenghaha/Projects/New_Agent_understandability_improvement/data/original/commons-codec/manual/testcases/SoundexTest/SoundexTest_testWikipediaAmericanSoundex.java). The refactored code must be syntactically correct and compilable against the provided CUT signatures. Do not alter the runtime behaviour of the original test: the same methods must be called with the same arguments and produce the same expected outcomes.\n"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I'll write the improved test file.The improved test compiles successfully. The refactored version replaces the six individual `assertEquals` calls with a single `@ParameterizedTest` driven by `@CsvSource`, making the test data-table structure explicit and giving each run a descriptive display name (`soundex(\"Robert\") == \"R163\"`). A class-level Javadoc and inline bullet comments explain the phonetic groupings (why Robert/Rupert share R163, how the silent letters in Ashcraft/Ashcroft are handled, etc.) without changing any method calls, arguments, or expected values."
    }
